      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_number": 1,
          "slide_label": "Slide 1",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "6 things I wish I knew before training"
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 2,
          "slide_label": "Slide 2",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "save this. you'll need it at the gym"
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 3,
          "slide_label": "Slide 3",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "1. Triceps\nwant your arm looking wider? focus on triceps way more than biceps."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 4,
          "slide_label": "Slide 4",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "2. Chest\nprogressively add weight, and don't push bench to failure every set. fatigue stacks up on you over time."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 5,
          "slide_label": "Slide 5",
          "is_metafi_slide": true,
          "text": "the real key: log your lifts and know exactly what to train\ntry the app"
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 6,
          "slide_label": "Slide 6",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "3. Back\nnot a muscle where you just grab the heaviest weight and go. lighten it up, control the movement, keep your form clean."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 7,
          "slide_label": "Slide 7",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "4. Biceps\ncable work felt way better than dumbbells for biceps for me."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 8,
          "slide_label": "Slide 8",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "5. Legs and abs\ndon't be scared to hit quads and hamstrings hard. and train your lower back too. makes a huge difference in your stability."
        }
      ]
    },
